{
 "result": "maze.py is a flat-array breadth-first search. It reads the grid from stdin, pads it with a '#' border so neighbour indexing needs no bounds checks, and walks the frontier level by level until it reaches E, printing the step count or -1. It matches all three public samples (2008, -1, 78). The assay is accepted with baseline median 4.25917 and noise 11.5%. I stopped here rather than spend energy on variants: a further gain must beat the baseline by more than 11.5%, and the obvious speedups (bidirectional search, numpy) are unverified and could break correctness.",
